<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Radziwiłł family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Radziwiłł</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Radziwiłł family was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, prominent from the fifteenth century. Raised to princes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in the sixteenth century, its members held the highest offices of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and vast estates centred on Nesvizh and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slutsk">Slutsk</a>. Barbara Radziwiłł married King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-ii-augustus">Sigismund II Augustus</a>, and the family remained among the richest in Poland-Lithuania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/radziwill-family.jpg" alt="Radziwiłł family" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape by Bastianowa (Bastiana) na podstawie: . Juliusz Ostrowsk... · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POL_COA_Radziwi%C5%82%C5%82_Ksi%C4%85%C5%BC%C4%99_Ia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
